# Derived awaiting-you queue — rewritten by each /pm-loop tick from
# projects/*/tasks/*.md. A view, not source; never commit it. Delete the file
# itself to turn the queue off (the loop never recreates it).
AWAITING.md

# Derived board snapshot — rewritten by scripts/write-snapshot.sh at the end of each
# /pm-loop tick, and read by scripts/build-board.sh (possibly from another instance).
# A view, not source. Delete the file itself to take this instance off the board (the
# writer never recreates it), and note the board HTML is derived output too.
SNAPSHOT.json
board.html

# The derived and per-machine paths every instance ignores — the `/repos/` view of the
# group's product repos, the board's local page and its other-owners cache, the
# per-machine identity override (`instance.config.local.json`), and the derived
# navigation indexes. install.sh manages the list between the markers below and
# REWRITES it on every stamp, so an entry added to the template reaches an instance
# stamped a year ago and not only a fresh one. Do not edit between the markers by hand;
# instance-local rules go outside them, where a stamp never touches them.
#
# The list lives in install.sh and NOT here, and that is not an oversight. THIS FILE IS
# ITSELF AN ACTIVE .gitignore INSIDE THE ai-bridge TEMPLATE'S OWN `seed/` DIRECTORY, so
# a `/index.md` line here matches `seed/index.md` and silently stops the template from
# tracking its own seed file. (Measured: it broke the upgrade.sh fixture, which re-inits
# a repo over a copy of seed/.) An EMPTY marker pair carries no pattern and has no such
# hazard. It also keeps ONE home for the list: seed content lands on a first stamp only,
# so a line that lived here as well would reach fresh installs twice and old ones never.
# `knowledge/index.md` is deliberately NOT ignored anywhere — it is the KB's curated
# lookup surface, it changes only when the KB changes, and an agent told to scan it
# needs it present in a fresh clone.
# >>> ai-bridge instance ignores >>>
# <<< ai-bridge instance ignores <<<

# Generic machinery is symlinked in from the ai-bridge template by
# install.sh and must NOT be committed here (it dangles on other machines).
# install.sh manages the list between the markers below — do not edit by hand.
# >>> ai-bridge machinery (symlinked) >>>
# <<< ai-bridge machinery <<<
